 The debug panel can save a bounded allowlisted JSONL snapshot on a background thread in the local Logs/InteractionDiagnostics directory. The snapshot identifies pending ingress and lost events. It includes the build's stamped Git SHA and Cargo profile when available, a sanitized requested asset-profile name captured at recorder installation, and a SHA-1 hash of the executable file read during export. The hash identifies the file on disk at export time, which could have been replaced since process start. Dirty source state and effective asset profile remain unknown. Existing snapshots are never intentionally overwritten.
 
-The inspector summarizes the most recent local action boundary and displays refusal reasons. Slot additions and explicit quest-ID failure events are matched heuristically by quest, scope and a provisional 30-second observation window. The window is not a measured server timeout. A missing journal model projection is unverified, and no displayed row is asserted. The quest selection receipt clears the acted latch only after a confirmed refusal for the same panel. Unconfirmed writes retain the latch and instruct the player to check the connection. The world interaction dispatcher carries a local ID through questgiver-open channel admission, outbox and socket-write reporting. The later panel observation is not yet matched to the action. Server refusals lacking a quest ID remain unassigned.
-
